000000000000.********************************************
000000000000:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/OBJLVL'.
000000000000Object Control Level (OBJLVL) - Help
000000000000
000000000000:XH3.Object Control Level (OBJLVL)
000000000000
000000000000:P.
000000000000The object control level of the object should be a unique
000000000000identifier that is changed with every changes applied to the object.
000000000000:P.
000000000000The object control level is used by the change management software
000000000000to store the task number that the object was assigned to.
000000000000:P.
000000000000:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
000000000000:P.
000000000000:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.
000000000000
000000000000:PARML.
000000000000:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
000000000000:PD.The object control level does not change.
000000000000:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
000000000000:PD.The object control level is not specified.
000000000000:PT.:PV.The object control level:EPV.
000000000000:PD.Specify the object control level of the object.
000000000000:EPARML.
000000000000:EHELP.
000000000000
000000000000.********************************************
000000000000.*  Keyword:  LICPGM
000000000000.********************************************
000000000000:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/LICPGM'.
000000000000Licensed program (LICPGM) - Help
000000000000
000000000000:XH3.Licensed program (LICPGM)
000000000000
000000000000:P.
000000000000If the object is part of a licensed program, then this
000000000000field shows the product number and the level of the
000000000000licensed program.
000000000000:P.
000000000000:LINES.
000000000000Position  1- 7:  Licensed program identifier
000000000000Position  8- 9:  Version
000000000000Position 10-11:  Release
000000000000Position 12-13:  Modification level
000000000000:ELINES.
000000000000:P.
000000000000The licensed program is used by the change management software
000000000000to store the modification level of the object.
000000000000:P.
000000000000:LINES.
000000000000Position  1- 3:  Version (*MAJOR)
000000000000Position     4:  Point   (.)
000000000000Position  5- 7:  Version (*MINOR)
000000000000Position  8- 9:  Release
000000000000Position    10:  Point   (.)
000000000000Position 11-12:  Level
000000000000Position    13:  not used
000000000000:ELINES.
000000000000:P.
000000000000:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
000000000000:P.
000000000000:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.
000000000000
000000000000:PARML.
000000000000:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
000000000000:PD.The licensed program does not change.
000000000000:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
000000000000:PD.The licensed program is not specified.
000000000000:PT.:PV.Licensed-program:EPV.
000000000000:PD.Specify the license program that the object is part of.
000000000000:EPARML.
000000000000:EHELP.
000000000000
000000000000.********************************************
000000000000.*  Keyword:  PTF
000000000000.********************************************
000000000000:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/PTF'.
000000000000PTF number (PTF) - Help
000000000000
000000000000:XH3.PTF number (PTF)
000000000000
000000000000:P.
000000000000The Program Temporary Fix that resulted in the creation of
000000000000the displayed object.
000000000000:P.
000000000000The PTF number is used by the change management software
000000000000to store the form number that moved the object.
000000000000:P.
000000000000
000000000000:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
000000000000:P.
000000000000:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.
000000000000
000000000000:PARML.
000000000000:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
000000000000:PD.The PTF number does not change.
000000000000:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
000000000000:PD.The PTF number is not specified.
000000000000:PT.:PV.PTF number:EPV.
000000000000:PD.The Program Temporary Fix that resulted in the creation of
000000000000the displayed object.
000000000000:EPARML.
000000000000:EHELP.
000000000000
000000000000.********************************************
000000000000.*  Keyword:  APAR
000000000000.********************************************
000000000000:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/APAR'.
000000000000APAR ID (APAR) - Help
000000000000
000000000000:XH3.APAR ID (APAR)
000000000000
000000000000:P.
000000000000The displayed object has been patched as the result of the
000000000000Authorized Program Analysis Report (APAR) with this
000000000000identification number.
000000000000:P.
000000000000The APAR ID is used by the change management software
000000000000to store the application ID the object is part of.
000000000000:P.
000000000000:LINES.
000000000000Position  1- 4:  Application
000000000000Position  5- 6:  unknown
000000000000:ELINES.
000000000000:P.
000000000000
000000000000:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
000000000000:P.
000000000000:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.
000000000000
000000000000:PARML.
000000000000:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
000000000000:PD.The APAR ID does not change.
000000000000:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
000000000000:PD.The APAR ID is not specified.
000000000000:PT.:PV.APAR-ID:EPV.
000000000000:PD.The APAR ID that resulted in the creation of
000000000000the displayed object.
000000000000:EPARML.
000000000000:EHELP.
000000000000
000000000000.********************************************
000000000000.*  Keyword:  USRDFNATR
000000000000.********************************************
000000000000:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/USRDFNATR'.
000000000000Benutzerdefiniertes Attribut (USRDFNATR) - Help
000000000000
000000000000:XH3.User-defined attribute (USRDFNATR)
000000000000
000000000000:P.
000000000000The user-defined attribute can be used to identifies
000000000000an object type further.
000000000000:P.
000000000000The user-defined attribute is used by the change management software
000000000000to store the type code the object is part of.
000000000000:P.
000000000000
000000000000:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
000000000000:P.
000000000000:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.
000000000000
000000000000:PARML.
000000000000:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
000000000000:PD.The user-defined attribute does not change
000000000000:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
000000000000:PD.The user-defined attribute is not specified.
000000000000:PT.:PV.User-defined attribute :EPV.
000000000000:PD.The user-defined attribute that specifies the object further.
000000000000:EPARML.
000000000000:EHELP.
